ity (`strict_mono_thm`), self-divisibility and factor divisibility (`dvd_thm`, `dvd_of_le_thm`), evenness for $n \\ge 2$ (`even_thm`), and lower bound $n! \\ge n$ (`ge_self_thm`).\n- **Post-condition, PBTs, and Correctness Theorem ([16_MyFactorial.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/16_MyFactorial.lean#L317-L456))**:\n  - `Post_prop` defined as the conjunction of all unary properties.\n  - Randomized Plausible PBTs (`#eval Plausible.Testable.check ...`) and bounded exhaustive PBTs (`example : (List.range ...).all ... = true := by native_decide`) for every property and `Post_prop`.\n  - `correctness_thm (n : Int) (h : Pre n) : Post_prop n`.\n- **Imperative Implementation, Tests, and Equivalence ([16_MyFactorial.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/16_MyFactorial.lean#L458-L545))**:\n  - Imperative implementations `progImp`, `myFactorialImp`, and `factorialNatImp` using `Id.run do` with mutable `result` and `for i in [1 : ...]` loops.\n  - Proven equivalence theorems `prog_eq_progImp`, `equivalence_thm : prog = progImp`, `myFactorial_eq_myFactorialImp`, and `factorialNat_eq_factorialNatImp`."}
